  offerDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Now that you understand how a truss bridge works and why equilibrium matters,
      let's put that knowledge to use.
    - For this project, you'll construct a bridge that can safely carry a vehicle
      across the training ground.
    - The required live load is <b><#E09500>400 kilograms</color></b>.
    - You'll use the Wood Road for the crossing surface and the newly unlocked Wood
      Beams to create a truss structure.
    - The connected members must work together to support the roadway and transfer
      the load toward the supports.
    - During the test, a vehicle will cross the bridge to test its structural stability.
    - <b><#E09500>Pay attention to how the connected members and supports respond as
      the vehicle crosses</color></b>.
    - I'll guide you through the construction process and show you a few more tools.
    - Just like your first project, you'll have a short <b><#E09500>quiz</color></b>
      after completing this training.
    - You can review your <b><#E09500>lessons in the Almanac</color></b> before starting.
    - If you're ready, take the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - You've accepted your second training contract.
    - This time, the roadway alone won't be enough for the design we're practicing.
    - You'll use the Wood Beams to form triangular arrangements that help support
      the crossing.
    - Remember what we discussed about equilibrium.
    - <b><#E09500>The structure must remain balanced and its members must safely carry
      the vehicle's weight</color></b>.
    - Now, follow the path to the <b><#E09500>Blueprint</color></b> and begin construction.
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - You've accepted your second training contract.
    - Use the Wood Beams to form triangular arrangements that help support the crossing.
    - Remember equilibrium. The structure must remain balanced and its members must
      safely carry the vehicle's weight.
    - Follow the path to the <b><#E09500>Blueprint</color></b> to begin constructing
      your Truss Bridge.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Excellent work, {PlayerName}.
    - You've now built your first <b><#E09500>Truss Bridge</color></b>.
    - You learned how connected structural members can work together to support a bridge.
    - You also learned how to <b><#E09500>select</color></b>, <b><#E09500>copy</color></b>,
      and <b><#E09500>paste</color></b> structural components.
    - Those tools will become useful when your designs become more complicated.
    - There are still more building tools to discover as your projects become more challenging.
